From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: wevtsvc: audit events from the Linux side reach the Security log

Signing in and out and elevation happen outside Windows, in PAM and in
sg-session's elevation broker, so nothing ever wrote the Security log (0143
left it empty unless SYSTEM reported something).

The Event Log service now imports audit events from a spool: a Unix
directory (HKLM\...\EventLog\Security AuditSpool, default
/var/lib/stained-glass-audit) that only root and SYSTEM's account may write
-- sg-session creates it 0700. Each file is one event, a few "KEY value"
lines (ID, TYPE success|failure, CATEGORY, TIME, SID, SOURCE, STRING...);
the service moves the files into the Security log once a second, in name
order, and deletes them; dot-names (still being written) are left alone,
anything that is not an event is dropped.

wevtsvc.dll's message table words the events (4624 logon, 4625 failed logon,
4634 logoff, 4648 explicit credentials, 4672 special privileges; categories
Logon, Logoff, Account Lockout, Special Logon -- our own wording), and
wine.inf registers it for the Microsoft-Windows-Security-Auditing source.

Gate: test/audit-gate.sh (make test-audit).
---
--- a/dlls/wevtsvc/wevtsvc.c
+++ b/dlls/wevtsvc/wevtsvc.c
@@ -37,9 +37,11 @@
 
